Betano owner Kaizen Gaming enters the Philippines, its first market in Asia

Kaizen Gaming will offer online sports betting and casino in the Philippines under a licence overseen by the Philippine Amusement and Gaming Corporation (PAGCOR). No launch date has been set. Kaizen calls itself the first multinational, fully regulated B2C iGaming operator to enter the market under PAGCOR's licensing framework, and says the Philippines is the only country in Asia with a broad, nationally authorised framework for online gaming. The move puts the company on five continents: Europe, North and South America, Africa and now Asia. Earlier this year it entered Ghana and Nigeria, and Betano is the official sponsor of Euro 2028.

